# T-14 LAUNCHPAD. `npm run lint` (prettier --check .) is scoped to code under active workspace
# development, not the whole repo. Two categories are deliberately excluded, not overlooked:
#
# 1. Frozen / not-ours-to-touch: types.ts and constants.ts are FROZEN per INTERFACES.md and
#    PROJECT.md — no task may edit them, including to reformat. reference/ is read-only source
#    material (see reference/README.md), never edited, never imported.
# 2. Narrative docs owned by nobody in particular / predate any task's formatting pass: the
#    root docs and tasks/*.md are planning documents, not code; results/*.md are per-task report
#    files (prose, not lint targets). None of these are "code style" in the sense this script
#    contract exists for, and several are outside this task's file ownership entirely.
#
# Verified against a pristine checkout: `prettier --check .` without this file flags these same
# 23 files (plus whatever any task's own unformatted source adds) — see notes/T-14-LAUNCHPAD/log.md.

